config FREETZ_PACKAGE_INFLUXDB3
	bool "InfluxDB 3.12.1 (experimental port)"
	select FREETZ_LIB_STDCXXLIB
	select FREETZ_LIB_libatomic
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3
	select FREETZ_LIB_libpython3
	select FREETZ_BUSYBOX_START_STOP_DAEMON
	select FREETZ_BUSYBOX_WGET
	default n
	help
		InfluxDB 3 Core time-series database with SQL and InfluxQL.
		This is an experimental source port, not a prebuilt 64-bit binary.
		All Freetz Rust target mappings are used, including 32-bit targets;
		selection alone does not certify architecture or runtime compatibility.
		Top-level cloud backend and jemalloc features are not selected;
		transitive dependencies may still contain these libraries.
		The embedded Python processing engine remains part of the server.
		WASM UDFs are unavailable on targets without native 64-bit atomics,
		including MIPS; requesting them returns an explicit unsupported error.
		Substantial RAM and persistent external storage are required.
		Includes a configuration page and rc.influxdb3 service script.
		Startup is disabled by default, with an authenticated loopback
		listener. Select an existing data directory before enabling it.